'\" t
.TH "ACTON\-VERIFY" "1"
.nh
.ad l
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "NAME"
acton\-verify \[em] Verify contract source code on the TON verifier service
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBacton verify\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcontract\-name\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Verify that a deployed contract address matches the local source code for a
contract from your project.
.sp
The verification flow compiles local sources, prepares data for the verifier
backend, collects the required signatures, and optionally submits the final
verification transaction to the blockchain.
.sp
With \fB\-\-new\fR, Acton uses a testnet\-only verifier. This flow requires a payment
before a new source bundle is uploaded.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.SS "Verify Options"
.sp
\fIcontract\-name\fR
.RS 4
Contract name to verify.
.sp
If omitted, Acton prompts when the project contains multiple contracts.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-address\fR \fIaddress\fR
.RS 4
Deployed contract address to verify.
.sp
If omitted, Acton prompts for it.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-wallet\fR \fIwallet\fR
.RS 4
Wallet to use for the verification transaction.
.sp
If omitted, Acton auto\-selects the only configured wallet or prompts when
multiple wallets are available.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-tonconnect\fR
.RS 4
Use TON Connect wallet approval for the verification transaction.
.sp
This uses the wallet selected in the browser.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-wallet\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-tonconnect\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Local TON Connect page port.
.sp
Defaults to \fB52258\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-compiler\-version\fR \fIversion\fR
.RS 4
Tolk compiler version to request on the verifier side.
.sp
Currently defaults to \fB1.4.2\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Run verification without submitting the final blockchain transaction.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-new\fR
.RS 4
Use the Acton verifier with a TON testnet spam payment.
.sp
This option conflicts with \fB\-\-net\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-payment\-tx\-hash\fR \fIpayment\-tx\-hash\fR
.RS 4
Reuse a finalized testnet payment transaction.
.sp
The transaction must contain the code hash from the current verification. This
option requires \fB\-\-new\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "Network Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-net\fR \fInetwork\fR
.RS 4
Network to verify against.
.sp
Defaults to \fBtestnet\fR\&.
.sp
This option conflicts with \fB\-\-new\fR\&. The Acton verifier always uses testnet.
.RE
.SH "TONCENTER API KEYS"
Built\-in \fBmainnet\fR/\fBtestnet\fR requests read \fBTONCENTER_MAINNET_API_KEY\fR or
\fBTONCENTER_TESTNET_API_KEY\fR, depending on \fB\-\-net\fR\&.
.sp
Acton loads \fB\&.env\fR automatically, so the simplest setup during project work is
usually to keep these keys there and use shell environment variables only for
one\-off overrides or CI.
.SS "Display Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIwhen\fR
.RS 4
Control when to use colored output.
.sp
Possible values: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR
.RE
.SS "Project Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the \fBActon.toml\fR file to use for this invocation.
.sp
Use this when running the command outside the project directory or when the
manifest lives at a non\-default location.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-project\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the project root to use for configuration discovery and relative
defaults.
.sp
This conflicts with \fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "PROCESS"
The built\-in verifier flow consists of:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'compiling the local contract
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'calculating the resulting code hash
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'sending sources to a verifier backend
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'collecting the required signatures
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'optionally sending the final verification transaction
.RE
.sp
Acton prepares the local compilation artifacts and uploads them to the
verification service. The final deployed\-code match is established by the
verifier flow itself; \fBacton verify\fR does not first perform a separate local
on\-chain code\-hash comparison against the target address before upload.
.sp
With \fB\-\-new\fR, the process is:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'Compile the local contract and compute its code hash.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'Request a ticket from \fB/api/v1/take\-ticket\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'Stop successfully if the code hash is already verified.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'Get wallet approval for the returned testnet amount and address.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'Send the payment with the returned code\-hash comment.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'Wait for the finalized recipient transaction.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 7.\h'+01'Upload the sources and recipient transaction hash to \fB/api/v1/verify\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "PREREQUISITES"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'a \fB\&.tolk\fR contract source in the current project
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'testnet funds when \fB\-\-new\fR is used without \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'a supported built\-in verifier network: \fBtestnet\fR or \fBmainnet\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'verifier backend availability for the selected network
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'a configured wallet or TON Connect wallet, funded when not using \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'reproducible compiler settings that match the deployed contract
.RE
.SH "CONTRACT AND WALLET SELECTION"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if \fB_contract\-name_\fR is omitted and exactly one contract is configured, Acton
selects it automatically
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if multiple contracts are configured, Acton prompts for the contract
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if \fB\-\-wallet\fR is omitted and exactly one wallet is configured, Acton selects
it automatically
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if multiple wallets are configured, Acton prompts for the wallet
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if \fB\-\-tonconnect\fR is used, Acton skips local wallet selection and uses the
wallet selected in the TON Connect page
.RE
.SH "REQUIREMENTS AND LIMITATIONS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'only \fB\&.tolk\fR sources can be verified
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'precompiled \fB\&.boc\fR contracts cannot be verified
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBlocalnet\fR and \fBcustom:<name>\fR are not supported by verifier backends
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-new\fR always uses testnet and does not accept \fB\-\-net\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'each new \fB\-\-new\fR verification payment contains the code hash in its comment
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'one payment transaction can authorize only one verification attempt
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'verification requires a funded local or TON Connect wallet when not using
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if a contract with the same code hash is already verified, the backend can
skip the final transaction
.RE
.SH "COST AND BACKEND NOTES"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'when \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR is not used, the final verification transaction sends
\fB0.1 GRAM\fR in the built\-in verifier flow
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'with \fB\-\-new\fR, the ticket defines the minimum testnet payment amount
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if the verifier backend reports that the contract is already verified, Acton
exits successfully without sending another transaction
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'on successful verification, Acton prints a verifier link for the contract
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES"
The verification flow also supports backend/debug environment overrides:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBACTON_VERIFY_BACKEND\fR overrides only the initial \fB/source\fR backend used for
source upload
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBACTON_VERIFY_BACKENDS\fR replaces the later signer \fB/sign\fR backend list
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBACTON_NEW_VERIFY_BACKEND\fR overrides the Acton verifier used by \fB\-\-new\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBACTON_VERIFY_DEBUG\fR enables verbose verification diagnostics by presence
alone
.RE
.sp
Backend override values are trimmed and normalized, including removal of a
trailing \fB/\fR\&.
.sp
With \fBACTON_VERIFY_DEBUG\fR, Acton prints:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'compiler version
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'collected source files
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'active source\-backend override
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'active signer\-backend override list
.RE
.sp
Example: debug source upload against a custom backend:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
ACTON_VERIFY_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:8080 \(rs
ACTON_VERIFY_DEBUG=1 \(rs
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-net mainnet \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.sp
Example: separate source upload from signer backends:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
ACTON_VERIFY_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:8080 \(rs
ACTON_VERIFY_BACKENDS=http://127.0.0.1:8081,http://127.0.0.1:8082 \(rs
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-net mainnet \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SH "DRY RUN"
For the built\-in verifier, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR uploads sources and collects signatures.
It skips the final blockchain transaction.
.sp
With \fB\-\-new\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR requests a ticket and prepares the source request. It
does not send a payment or upload sources.
.SH "TON CONNECT"
Use \fB\-\-tonconnect\fR to approve the final verification transaction through a TON
Connect wallet instead of a wallet configured in \fBwallets.toml\fR:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-net mainnet \-\-tonconnect
.fi
.RE
.sp
With \fB\-\-new\fR, do not pass \fB\-\-net\fR:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-new \-\-tonconnect
.fi
.RE
.sp
Acton starts a local TON Connect page and opens it in the browser. Use
\fB\-\-tonconnect\-port\fR when the default page port is already busy.
.SH "RETRIES AND FAILURE HINTS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'source upload is attempted up to 8 times total (initial try plus up to
7 retries) for transient transport failures and backend 5xx responses
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'retry backoff grows from 1 second to 7 seconds between attempts
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'backend error responses are printed with the response body when available
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'5xx failures suggest retrying later and using \fBACTON_VERIFY_DEBUG=1\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'backend problems can also be narrowed down by pointing
\fBACTON_VERIFY_BACKEND\fR at a specific endpoint
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'with \fB\-\-new\fR, only an explicitly retryable source storage failure permits
reuse of the same payment
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'other \fB\-\-new\fR results after the payment claim consume the payment, including
generic internal failures
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB0\fR: Verification completed successfully, including successful dry runs and
flows where the backend decides that no final transaction is needed.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB1\fR: Compilation failed, the verifier backend rejected the request, not
enough signatures were collected, wallet resolution failed, or a blockchain
transaction failed.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'Verify on testnet:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL...
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'Verify on mainnet:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address UQDt7LL... \-\-net mainnet
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'Use a specific wallet:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-wallet deployer
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'Test the flow without sending the final transaction:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'Verify with an explicit compiler version:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-address EQDt7LL... \-\-compiler\-version 1.2.0
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'Use the Acton testnet verifier:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-new \-\-wallet deployer
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 7.\h'+01'Retry an upload with an existing finalized payment:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton verify Counter \-\-new \-\-payment\-tx\-hash '<transaction\-hash>'
.fi
.RE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fIContract verification guide\fR <https://ton\-blockchain.github.io/acton/docs/verify>
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fIWallet management guide\fR <https://ton\-blockchain.github.io/acton/docs/wallets>
.RE
